window.CPY701 = {"course": "CPY 701 \u00b7 Introduction to Counseling Psychology", "programme": "Master's Degree in Counseling Psychology", "weeks": [{"id": "w01", "num": 1, "title": "The Nature and Concept of Counseling Psychology", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w01/01-title.png", "title": "Introduction to Counseling Psychology", "start": 0.0, "end": 30.59}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 30.59, "end": 66.84}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/03-working-picture.png", "title": "Counseling psychology: a working picture", "start": 66.84, "end": 115.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/04-definitions.png", "title": "Three definitions worth keeping", "start": 115.46, "end": 166.78}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/05-rogers.png", "title": "rogers", "start": 166.78, "end": 191.45}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/06-helping-continuum.png", "title": "The helping continuum", "start": 191.45, "end": 241.18}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/07-compare-three.png", "title": "Guidance, counseling and psychotherapy side by side", "start": 241.18, "end": 286.58}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/08-neighbours.png", "title": "Counseling psychology among its neighbours", "start": 286.58, "end": 336.84}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/09-core-values.png", "title": "Six values that give the specialty its character", "start": 336.84, "end": 379.14}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/10-scope.png", "title": "What counseling psychologists actually do", "start": 379.14, "end": 423.88}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/11-limits.png", "title": "Where competence ends and referral begins", "start": 423.88, "end": 470.79}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/12-spa-model.png", "title": "The scientist-practitioner-advocate identity", "start": 470.79, "end": 514.21}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/13-art-science.png", "title": "Counseling as science and as art", "start": 514.21, "end": 552.57}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/14-person-of-counselor.png", "title": "The person of the counselor", "start": 552.57, "end": 594.74}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 1 in review", "start": 594.74, "end": 632.63}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w01/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 632.63, "end": 674.87}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 5.85, "t": "Welcome to CPY 701, Introduction to Counseling Psychology, a core course in the Master's"}, {"s": 5.85, "e": 11.51, "t": "degree in Counseling Psychology. I am glad you are here. This is week one of sixteen,"}, {"s": 11.51, "e": 17.22, "t": "and in this first lecture we ask the most fundamental question of all: what exactly is"}, {"s": 17.22, "e": 22.55, "t": "counseling psychology? By the end of this session you will be able to define the"}, {"s": 22.55, "e": 28.33, "t": "specialty, place it on the helping continuum, and describe the values, scope and limits"}, {"s": 28.33, "e": 30.59, "t": "that govern professional practice."}, {"s": 30.59, "e": 36.05, "t": "Here is what this week promises. First, you will define counseling psychology from"}, {"s": 36.05, "e": 41.1, "t": "authoritative sources. Second, you will distinguish guidance, counseling and"}, {"s": 41.1, "e": 46.69, "t": "psychotherapy without confusing them. Third, you will explain the core values of the"}, {"s": 46.69, "e": 52.41, "t": "specialty and its scope of practice, including where your competence ends and referral"}, {"s": 52.41, "e": 58.2, "t": "begins. And fourth, you will describe the scientist, practitioner and advocate identity"}, {"s": 58.2, "e": 63.98, "t": "that this programme expects you to grow into. Keep these four outcomes beside you as we"}, {"s": 63.98, "e": 66.84, "t": "move; every slide today serves one of them."}, {"s": 66.84, "e": 72.56, "t": "Let us begin with a working picture. Counseling psychology is a professional specialty"}, {"s": 72.56, "e": 78.02, "t": "within psychology. It applies psychological theory, research and technique to help"}, {"s": 78.02, "e": 83.54, "t": "people improve their wellbeing, resolve problems in living, and develop personally,"}, {"s": 83.54, "e": 89.19, "t": "socially, educationally and vocationally. Notice three things in that sentence. It is"}, {"s": 89.19, "e": 95.04, "t": "professional: it is governed by training, ethics and regulation, not by good intentions."}, {"s": 95.04, "e": 100.83, "t": "It is psychological: it works through mental processes, behaviour and relationship, not"}, {"s": 100.83, "e": 106.61, "t": "through medicine or coercion. And it is helping: its engine is a deliberate, boundaried"}, {"s": 106.61, "e": 112.4, "t": "relationship between a trained counselor and a client who seeks change. Everything else"}, {"s": 112.4, "e": 115.46, "t": "in this course grows from those three anchors."}, {"s": 115.46, "e": 121.05, "t": "Now let three authoritative voices sharpen the definition. The Society of Counseling"}, {"s": 121.05, "e": 126.78, "t": "Psychology, Division 17 of the American Psychological Association, describes the field"}, {"s": 126.78, "e": 132.17, "t": "as a specialty that facilitates personal and interpersonal functioning across the"}, {"s": 132.17, "e": 137.76, "t": "lifespan, focusing on emotional, social, vocational, educational, health-related and"}, {"s": 137.76, "e": 143.28, "t": "developmental concerns. Corey reminds us that counseling is a collaborative process"}, {"s": 143.28, "e": 148.67, "t": "between two people, in which the counselor's attitudes and skills help the client"}, {"s": 148.67, "e": 154.26, "t": "examine and change behaviour. Gladding calls counseling the professional practice of"}, {"s": 154.26, "e": 160.12, "t": "helping people who are not severely disturbed to solve problems and make decisions. Hear"}, {"s": 160.12, "e": 165.98, "t": "the common thread: ordinary people, real problems, a trained helper, and change that the"}, {"s": 165.98, "e": 166.78, "t": "client owns."}, {"s": 166.78, "e": 172.5, "t": "Carl Rogers left us a line that captures the heart of our work: the curious paradox is"}, {"s": 172.5, "e": 178.28, "t": "that when I accept myself just as I am, then I can change. Counseling psychology is not"}, {"s": 178.28, "e": 184.07, "t": "about fixing broken people. It is about creating conditions in which a person, accepted"}, {"s": 184.07, "e": 189.78, "t": "and understood, can move toward their own potential. Hold that paradox; it will return"}, {"s": 189.78, "e": 191.45, "t": "in every theory we study."}, {"s": 191.45, "e": 196.83, "t": "Where does counseling sit on the helping road? Picture a continuum. At one end is"}, {"s": 196.83, "e": 202.62, "t": "guidance: informative, preventive and often educational, giving students or clients the"}, {"s": 202.62, "e": 208.4, "t": "information and direction they need, for example choosing a course or a career. Next is"}, {"s": 208.4, "e": 214.12, "t": "counseling: a deeper, relational process with clients who are experiencing adjustment,"}, {"s": 214.12, "e": 219.24, "t": "developmental or situational distress but remain within the range of ordinary"}, {"s": 219.24, "e": 224.36, "t": "functioning. Further along is psychotherapy: longer, more intensive work with"}, {"s": 224.36, "e": 229.95, "t": "deeper-seated personality or chronic emotional difficulties. And at the far end sits"}, {"s": 229.95, "e": 235.67, "t": "psychiatric and medical treatment, where diagnosis and medication lead. The boundaries"}, {"s": 235.67, "e": 241.18, "t": "blur in practice, but the direction of travel, depth, duration and training differ."}, {"s": 241.18, "e": 246.9, "t": "Let us make those differences concrete. Guidance is typically brief, informational and"}, {"s": 246.9, "e": 252.68, "t": "preventive; its client is often a student or a group; a teacher or guidance officer may"}, {"s": 252.68, "e": 258.2, "t": "deliver it. Counseling is relational and focused on present problems in living; its"}, {"s": 258.2, "e": 263.91, "t": "client is a person or couple in situational distress; the counselor holds postgraduate"}, {"s": 263.91, "e": 269.56, "t": "professional training. Psychotherapy runs longer, works with more entrenched patterns"}, {"s": 269.56, "e": 275.28, "t": "and often with diagnosed disorders; the psychotherapist or clinical psychologist leads"}, {"s": 275.28, "e": 280.93, "t": "it. Memorise the table's dimensions, focus, client, duration, depth and practitioner,"}, {"s": 280.93, "e": 286.58, "t": "because examination questions love to ask you to distinguish these three in practice."}, {"s": 286.58, "e": 292.23, "t": "A frequent confusion: how is counseling psychology different from clinical psychology"}, {"s": 292.23, "e": 297.48, "t": "and psychiatry? We share much: assessment, diagnostic awareness, evidence-based"}, {"s": 297.48, "e": 302.93, "t": "intervention, and ethics. What distinguishes us is emphasis. Counseling psychology"}, {"s": 302.93, "e": 308.59, "t": "stresses strengths and resources, not only pathology; it works with developmental and"}, {"s": 308.59, "e": 314.3, "t": "vocational concerns as seriously as with disorder; it favours brief, focal, preventive"}, {"s": 314.3, "e": 320.02, "t": "intervention; and it treats culture, context and social justice as clinical facts, not"}, {"s": 320.02, "e": 325.74, "t": "footnotes. Psychiatry adds medical training and prescribing; clinical psychology leans"}, {"s": 325.74, "e": 331.52, "t": "harder on severe psychopathology and assessment batteries. Knowing the overlap protects"}, {"s": 331.52, "e": 336.84, "t": "you from turf wars; knowing the distinction protects your professional identity."}, {"s": 336.84, "e": 342.5, "t": "Six values give the specialty its character. Wellness and prevention: we would rather"}, {"s": 342.5, "e": 348.15, "t": "strengthen a community than only repair damage. Strengths and resilience: we hunt for"}, {"s": 348.15, "e": 353.8, "t": "resources, not merely deficits. Development across the lifespan: a twelve-year-old, a"}, {"s": 353.8, "e": 359.59, "t": "forty-year-old and a seventy-year-old face different tasks, and we meet each where they"}, {"s": 359.59, "e": 365.18, "t": "are. Multicultural and social justice commitment: culture, faith, gender and poverty"}, {"s": 365.18, "e": 370.76, "t": "shape distress and help-seeking. Brief, focal, evidence-informed practice: we choose"}, {"s": 370.76, "e": 376.42, "t": "what works, and we measure it. And advocacy: sometimes the most therapeutic act is to"}, {"s": 376.42, "e": 379.14, "t": "change the system that wounds the client."}, {"s": 379.14, "e": 384.4, "t": "What does the scope of practice look like on the ground? Populations: children,"}, {"s": 384.4, "e": 390.26, "t": "adolescents, students, couples, families, workers and older adults. Concerns: adjustment"}, {"s": 390.26, "e": 396.05, "t": "to change, academic and examination stress, career decision-making, grief, relationship"}, {"s": 396.05, "e": 401.58, "t": "conflict, mild to moderate anxiety and depression, trauma reactions, health-related"}, {"s": 401.58, "e": 406.84, "t": "adjustment, and substance-use concerns at an early stage. Settings: schools and"}, {"s": 406.84, "e": 412.36, "t": "universities, hospitals and clinics, workplaces and employee assistance programmes,"}, {"s": 412.36, "e": 417.36, "t": "rehabilitation centres, faith and community organisations, non-governmental"}, {"s": 417.36, "e": 423.22, "t": "organisations, and private or telepractice. Wide, yes. Unlimited, no. And that brings us"}, {"s": 423.22, "e": 423.88, "t": "to limits."}, {"s": 423.88, "e": 429.2, "t": "Competence has edges, and naming them is a professional act, not a confession of"}, {"s": 429.2, "e": 434.93, "t": "weakness. Refer onward when you meet psychosis or severe mood disorder with risk; when"}, {"s": 434.93, "e": 440.58, "t": "medical causes may explain the presentation; when the client needs medication review;"}, {"s": 440.58, "e": 446.3, "t": "when forensic or custody questions arise; when the problem exceeds your training, such"}, {"s": 446.3, "e": 451.96, "t": "as specialist eating-disorder or addiction treatment; and whenever your own values or"}, {"s": 451.96, "e": 457.42, "t": "relationship with the client compromise objectivity. Equally, refer in: counseling"}, {"s": 457.42, "e": 463.27, "t": "psychologists work inside multidisciplinary teams, and a warm referral letter is part of"}, {"s": 463.27, "e": 468.93, "t": "the intervention. If you ever feel unsure whether a case is yours, supervision exists"}, {"s": 468.93, "e": 470.79, "t": "precisely for that question."}, {"s": 470.79, "e": 476.31, "t": "So who are you becoming? The classic answer is the scientist, practitioner, and, in"}, {"s": 476.31, "e": 481.89, "t": "newer formulations, the advocate. As scientist you consume and produce evidence: you"}, {"s": 481.89, "e": 487.48, "t": "read outcome research, you measure your own results, you stay humble before data. As"}, {"s": 487.48, "e": 493.33, "t": "practitioner you translate that evidence into skilful, timely, humane action with a real"}, {"s": 493.33, "e": 498.98, "t": "person in front of you. As advocate you notice that some suffering is manufactured by"}, {"s": 498.98, "e": 504.83, "t": "unjust systems, and you act to change conditions, in schools, workplaces and policy. The"}, {"s": 504.83, "e": 510.69, "t": "gold centre of this triangle is you: the integrated counseling psychologist, holding all"}, {"s": 510.69, "e": 514.21, "t": "three roles without letting any one of them dominate."}, {"s": 514.21, "e": 519.53, "t": "Is counseling an art or a science? The honest answer is both, and the tension is"}, {"s": 519.53, "e": 524.85, "t": "creative. The science side gives you theory, technique, measurement and research"}, {"s": 524.85, "e": 530.56, "t": "evidence: what to do, in what order, with what expected effect. The art side gives you"}, {"s": 530.56, "e": 536.35, "t": "timing, presence, language and intuition: knowing when to be silent, when to challenge,"}, {"s": 536.35, "e": 541.8, "t": "when a metaphor will land where a lecture would bounce off. Science without art is"}, {"s": 541.8, "e": 547.51, "t": "mechanical and cold; art without science is charming but unaccountable. Our discipline"}, {"s": 547.51, "e": 552.57, "t": "asks you to be rigorous enough to be trusted and human enough to be helpful."}, {"s": 552.57, "e": 558.22, "t": "Finally this week, a preview of the person of the counselor. Technical skill will not"}, {"s": 558.22, "e": 564.01, "t": "carry you if the person behind the skill is unexamined. The qualities we will cultivate"}, {"s": 564.01, "e": 569.79, "t": "across this programme include self-awareness and honesty about your own wounds; warmth,"}, {"s": 569.79, "e": 575.65, "t": "respect and genuineness; emotional stability and the capacity to tolerate another's pain"}, {"s": 575.65, "e": 580.97, "t": "without collapsing or fleeing; openness to culture and difference; courage to be"}, {"s": 580.97, "e": 586.42, "t": "challenged and to change; and a disciplined ethical conscience. Start a reflective"}, {"s": 586.42, "e": 592.14, "t": "journal now, this week. One page after every skills practice. By week fifteen you will"}, {"s": 592.14, "e": 594.74, "t": "see a counselor forming in those pages."}, {"s": 594.74, "e": 600.25, "t": "Let us gather the week. Counseling psychology applies psychological science to help"}, {"s": 600.25, "e": 605.97, "t": "people improve functioning and wellbeing across the lifespan. It sits between guidance"}, {"s": 605.97, "e": 611.76, "t": "and psychotherapy on the helping continuum, distinguished by focus, depth, duration and"}, {"s": 611.76, "e": 617.61, "t": "training. It shares ground with clinical psychology and psychiatry while keeping its own"}, {"s": 617.61, "e": 623.06, "t": "emphasis on strengths, development, prevention and culture. Its scope is broad but"}, {"s": 623.06, "e": 628.71, "t": "bounded, and referral is a skill, not a failure. And it is lived through a scientist,"}, {"s": 628.71, "e": 632.63, "t": "practitioner, advocate identity held by an examined person."}, {"s": 632.63, "e": 637.82, "t": "Your task before next week. Write your own sixty-word definition of counseling"}, {"s": 637.82, "e": 643.34, "t": "psychology, then defend it in one paragraph against the strongest objection you can"}, {"s": 643.34, "e": 648.79, "t": "imagine. Second, observe one helping conversation in your community, a teacher and"}, {"s": 648.79, "e": 654.45, "t": "student, a pastor and a member, a friend and a friend, and note which helping mode it"}, {"s": 654.45, "e": 660.1, "t": "was: guidance, counseling, or something else. Bring both to the seminar. Next week we"}, {"s": 660.1, "e": 665.89, "t": "travel through history, from Frank Parsons to the first graduate training in counseling"}, {"s": 665.89, "e": 671.74, "t": "psychology in Nigeria. Read Corey and Gladding's history chapters before then. Thank you"}, {"s": 671.74, "e": 674.87, "t": "for your attention; I will see you in week two."}], "mode": "captions", "duration": 674.87}, {"id": "w02", "num": 2, "title": "Historical and Philosophical Development", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w02/01-title.png", "title": "Historical and Philosophical Development", "start": 0.0, "end": 34.53}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 34.53, "end": 69.98}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/03-why-history.png", "title": "Why a whole week on history?", "start": 69.98, "end": 112.25}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/04-timeline-1.png", "title": "How the specialty was seeded", "start": 112.25, "end": 165.88}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/05-timeline-2.png", "title": "How the specialty grew up", "start": 165.88, "end": 216.81}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/06-figures.png", "title": "The ancestors, briefly", "start": 216.81, "end": 268.86}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/07-great-debate.png", "title": "Rogers versus Williamson: the debate that built our habits", "start": 268.86, "end": 309.42}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/08-parsons-quote.png", "title": "parsons-quote", "start": 309.42, "end": 337.64}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/09-indigenous-helping.png", "title": "Indigenous and faith-based helping systems", "start": 337.64, "end": 389.65}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/10-nigeria-formal.png", "title": "Counseling psychology in Nigeria: five movements", "start": 389.65, "end": 439.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/11-two-histories.png", "title": "Two histories, one profession", "start": 439.06, "end": 491.48}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/12-assumptions.png", "title": "The assumptions underneath the history", "start": 491.48, "end": 538.88}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/13-six-isms.png", "title": "Six commitments that decode every theory", "start": 538.88, "end": 580.51}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/14-obligations.png", "title": "What history obligates you to do", "start": 580.51, "end": 620.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 2 in review", "start": 620.46, "end": 660.91}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w02/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 660.91, "end": 700.24}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.94, "t": "Welcome back to CPY 701. Week one gave us a definition; week two gives us a memory."}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.96, "t": "Today we trace how counseling psychology came to be, from Frank Parsons's vocational"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.91, "t": "bureau in Boston in 1908, through the mental hygiene movement and the wars, to Carl"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.64, "t": "Rogers's quiet revolution, and then home: to Nigeria, where graduate training in"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.94, "t": "counseling psychology began at the University of Nigeria, Nsukka in 1994. History is not"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.52, "t": "decoration in this course; it explains why we practice as we do."}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.47, "t": "Four outcomes for this week. One, construct a timeline of the field from vocational"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.7, "t": "guidance to the present. Two, identify the contribution of key figures: Parsons, Beers,"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.65, "t": "Rogers, Williamson and Super. Three, explain how counseling psychology developed in"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.45, "t": "Nigeria and Africa, including regulation and the Mental Health Act of 2022. Four,"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.54, "t": "articulate the philosophical assumptions, humanistic, phenomenological, developmental"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.98, "t": "and contextual, that undergird our practice. Keep them in view as we travel."}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.08, "t": "Why spend a whole week on history at master's level? Because every technique you will"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.26, "t": "learn carries an argument inside it. When you reflect feeling, you are taking Rogers's"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.07, "t": "side in a debate that began in the 1940s. When you screen a client, you inherit a"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.17, "t": "psychometric tradition born in army camps in 1917. When you advocate for a community,"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.98, "t": "you continue the prevention movement of the 1960s. History tells you what you are"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.16, "t": "standing on, so that you can stand deliberately rather than by habit. It also protects"}, {"s": 0.16, "e": 0.26, "t": "you from chronological snobbery: old does not mean false, and new does not mean true."}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.14, "t": "Begin at the beginning. 1908, Boston: Frank Parsons opens the Vocations Bureau and"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.25, "t": "proposes that wise career choice rests on self-knowledge, occupational knowledge, and"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.28, "t": "true reasoning between them, the seed of trait-and-factor counseling. The same year,"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.02, "t": "Clifford Beers turns his own asylum experience into the mental hygiene movement,"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.62, "t": "planting prevention and humane reform. 1917 to 1918: the First World War makes"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.22, "t": "psychological testing industrial-scale with the Army Alpha and Beta batteries;"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.53, "t": "assessment enters public life. 1942: Carl Rogers publishes Counseling and Psychotherapy,"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.85, "t": "and the client, not the diagnosis, moves to the centre. 1946: the American Psychological"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.88, "t": "Association charts Division 17, and counseling psychology becomes a named specialty."}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.91, "t": "The second half of the century professionalizes the specialty. From 1949 and 1951, the"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.88, "t": "Boulder conference's scientist-practitioner model and Veterans Administration funding"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.91, "t": "shape graduate training: the counselor as both researcher and clinician. The community"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.38, "t": "mental health movement of the 1960s pushes practice out of the clinic and into"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.06, "t": "communities, strengthening prevention and outreach. The 1970s and 1980s bring the"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.81, "t": "developmental turn: lifespan growth, wellness and vocational development become as"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.99, "t": "central as remediation. Then the multicultural turn of the 1980s and 1990s makes culture"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.81, "t": "and social justice clinical necessities. And our own century adds outcome research,"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.81, "t": "measurement-based care, teletherapy and digital practice."}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.7, "t": "Meet the ancestors briefly. Frank Parsons, engineer and reformer, gave us vocational"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.59, "t": "matching and the very idea of systematic guidance. Clifford Beers, a former patient,"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.07, "t": "gave us the moral impulse: humane care and prevention. Carl Rogers gave us the"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.75, "t": "relationship: empathy, congruence and unconditional positive regard as measurable"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.64, "t": "conditions of change. Edward G. Williamson, at Minnesota, defended a more directive,"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.25, "t": "structured trait-and-factor approach, and the Rogers-Williamson debate trained a"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.07, "t": "generation to think about method. Donald Super gave career development its lifespan"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.11, "t": "psychology. And in Nigeria, the pioneers who opened postgraduate training at Nsukka in"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.86, "t": "1994 gave our own context its first cohort of home-grown counseling psychologists."}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.88, "t": "That Rogers-Williamson debate deserves a slide of its own, because it created our"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.22, "t": "professional habit of arguing with evidence. Williamson's Minnesota point of view held"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.3, "t": "that clients benefit from structured, directive guidance: assessment, information,"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.76, "t": "advice where warranted. Rogers held that the client carries the capacity for change, and"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.09, "t": "the counselor's job is to provide conditions, not directions. The field did not simply"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.12, "t": "pick a side; it learned to test. From that quarrel came outcome research, process"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.45, "t": "research, and the scientist-practitioner compact that still governs us: research feeds"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.42, "t": "practice, and practice poses the questions research must answer."}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.69, "t": "Parsons left us the cleanest statement of the early vision, and it still reads like a"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.09, "t": "counseling contract: three factors enter into wise career choice, a clear understanding"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.24, "t": "of yourself, a knowledge of the requirements and conditions of success in different"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.63, "t": "occupations, and true reasoning about the relations of these two groups of facts. Self,"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.03, "t": "context, and disciplined reflection between them: that is counseling in one sentence, a"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.64, "t": "century before our jargon."}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.38, "t": "Now bring the story home. Long before any bureau or clinic, African communities ran"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.39, "t": "sophisticated helping systems. The extended family and its elders mediated conflict and"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.2, "t": "guided the young; age grades and titles carried mentorship duties; religious leaders"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.87, "t": "offered counsel and meaning; traditional healers addressed distress in an idiom of"}, {"s": 0.87, "e": 0.47, "t": "spirit, ancestor and community. Communal philosophies, ubuntu in the south of the"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.86, "t": "continent, omoluwabi and similar ethics in Yoruba land, framed the person as a"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.74, "t": "person-through-others. These systems supplied continuity, meaning and accountability."}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.2, "t": "They also carried limits we must name: stigma around mental distress, spiritual"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.28, "t": "attribution that could delay medical care, and confidentiality norms very different from"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.63, "t": "ours."}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.71, "t": "Formal counseling psychology in Nigeria arrives in five movements. In the 1950s and 60s,"}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.8, "t": "post-independence school expansion creates guidance services and the teacher-counsellor."}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.6, "t": "Through the 1970s and 80s, universities establish guidance and counselling units and"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 1.0, "t": "departments, and professional associations form to set standards. In 1994, the"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.08, "t": "University of Nigeria, Nsukka begins postgraduate training in counseling psychology, the"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.54, "t": "moment our specialty acquires a graduate pipeline of its own. In the 2000s, the"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.63, "t": "Counsellors Registration Council of Nigeria brings statutory registration and standards."}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.64, "t": "And in 2022, the National Mental Health Act modernizes rights, services and integration"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.06, "t": "of mental health into general care."}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.75, "t": "Set the two histories side by side and the picture becomes honest. While Boston was"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.58, "t": "opening vocational bureaus and American armies were testing recruits, our context was"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.54, "t": "running indigenous and faith-based helping, and a colonial school system with no formal"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.44, "t": "guidance. While Division 17 professionalized and community mental health spread, newly"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.47, "t": "independent Nigeria was building school guidance and university counselling units. While"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.37, "t": "the global field turned multicultural and preventive, Nigeria was forming associations"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.99, "t": "and opening graduate training in 1994. And while today's global field argues about"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.61, "t": "evidence and teletherapy, Nigeria is consolidating regulation and research output."}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.51, "t": "Neither history is a footnote to the other; your practice lives at their intersection."}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.2, "t": "Beneath the history sit philosophical assumptions, and you should know yours. About"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.02, "t": "persons: we assume people are more than their diagnoses; that they possess choice and"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.99, "t": "agency, however constrained; that they carry a growth-oriented, self-righting tendency;"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.61, "t": "and that mind, body, culture and spirit interlock, so holism is not a slogan but a"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.16, "t": "method. About knowing and doing: we assume experience is best understood from the"}, {"s": 0.16, "e": 0.72, "t": "client's frame, which is phenomenology; that knowledge is provisional and must be"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.34, "t": "tested, which is the scientist-practitioner; that culture constitutes distress and"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.23, "t": "healing rather than decorating them; and that prevention, wherever possible, is kinder"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.88, "t": "and cheaper than repair."}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.77, "t": "Name the six commitments and you can read any counseling text with X-ray vision."}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.94, "t": "Humanism: the person is worthier than the problem. Phenomenology: the client's lived"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.12, "t": "experience is primary data. Developmentalism: behaviour makes sense against lifespan"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.6, "t": "tasks. Contextualism: context, culture, class and gender shape every session. Prevention"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 1.0, "t": "orientation: stop harm before it starts. Social justice: some distress is manufactured,"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.47, "t": "and counselors answer it with advocacy as well as empathy. Every theory we meet in weeks"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.52, "t": "four and five will be a different mixture of these six."}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.77, "t": "So what does history obligate you to do? Five things. Hold an identity: you inherit a"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.17, "t": "tradition with values, not a bag of tricks. Hold humility: every idea, including yours,"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.42, "t": "is dated and culturally located. Hold culture seriously: imported theories need local"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.67, "t": "validation before you trust them with a client in Ibadan or Kano. Hold advocacy: this"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.07, "t": "field grew whenever it answered a social need, and shrank whenever it did not. And hold"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.55, "t": "the conversation open: your research questions continue a century-long argument; join it"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.46, "t": "with evidence, not volume."}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.08, "t": "Gather the week. Counseling psychology grew from vocational guidance, psychometrics,"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.43, "t": "mental hygiene and the person-centred revolution into a named specialty in 1946,"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.04, "t": "professionalized through the scientist-practitioner model, and turned developmental,"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.33, "t": "multicultural and preventive across the late century. Nigeria's story runs from"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.94, "t": "indigenous and faith-based helping, through school guidance and university units, to"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.56, "t": "graduate training at Nsukka in 1994, statutory registration, and the National Mental"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.18, "t": "Health Act 2022. Underneath sit six philosophical commitments. History, in short, is"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.92, "t": "your professional grammar."}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.47, "t": "Your task before week three. Build a ten-event timeline that interleaves global and"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.09, "t": "Nigerian milestones, one sentence of significance per event; the interleaving is the"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.5, "t": "point. Second, write one philosophical assumption you personally hold about human"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.85, "t": "nature, then write how your counseling would change if it were false; bring both"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.4, "t": "paragraphs to the seminar. Read the history chapters in Corey and Gladding, plus at"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.02, "t": "least one scholarly account of counseling psychology's growth in Nigeria. Next week:"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.84, "t": "where we sit among the helping professions, and the ethics of referral. See you in week"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.24, "t": "three."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 700.24, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W02-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w02-captions.vtt"}, {"id": "w03", "num": 3, "title": "Relationship to Other Disciplines and Helping Professions", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w03/01-title.png", "title": "Among the Helping Professions", "start": 0.0, "end": 30.54}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 30.54, "end": 65.98}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/03-why-boundaries.png", "title": "Why professional boundaries matter", "start": 65.98, "end": 107.25}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/04-professions-table.png", "title": "Six helping professions at a glance", "start": 107.25, "end": 165.12}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/05-clinical-vs-counseling.png", "title": "Counseling psychology and clinical psychology", "start": 165.12, "end": 214.08}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/06-psychiatry.png", "title": "Psychiatry and the medical model", "start": 214.08, "end": 259.42}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/07-other-professions.png", "title": "Professions we work beside, not above", "start": 259.42, "end": 308.45}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/08-pastoral.png", "title": "Pastoral care: strengths, limits, collaboration", "start": 308.45, "end": 355.59}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/09-traditional-healers.png", "title": "Traditional healers: prevalence, reasons, ethics", "start": 355.59, "end": 413.17}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/10-referral-flow.png", "title": "The referral pathway in five moves", "start": 413.17, "end": 475.67}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/11-referral-ethics.png", "title": "The ethics of moving a client between worlds", "start": 475.67, "end": 525.69}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/12-teamwork.png", "title": "What we bring to the team, what we ask of it", "start": 525.69, "end": 571.69}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/13-no-health.png", "title": "no-health", "start": 571.69, "end": 607.11}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/14-identity-card.png", "title": "Your identity card: six distinctive contributions", "start": 607.11, "end": 649.86}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 3 in review", "start": 649.86, "end": 692.48}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w03/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 692.48, "end": 742.52}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.82, "t": "Welcome to week three of CPY 701. Last week we saw where the field came from; this week"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.63, "t": "we map where it sits. A profession is defined not only by what it does, but by what its"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.31, "t": "neighbours do, and by what it refuses to do. By the end of this lecture you should be"}, {"s": 0.31, "e": 0.06, "t": "able to place counseling psychology confidently among clinical psychology, psychiatry,"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.48, "t": "social work, nursing, pastoral care and traditional healing, and to move a client"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.55, "t": "between those worlds ethically."}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.43, "t": "Four outcomes. One, contrast counseling psychology with clinical psychology, psychiatry,"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.12, "t": "social work, nursing, pastoral care and traditional healing. Two, identify the unique"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.93, "t": "contributions of our specialty to multidisciplinary work. Three, map a referral network"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.68, "t": "for your own community, including the informal helping resources clients actually use."}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.23, "t": "Four, apply the ethics of referral: consent, warm handover, no abandonment, and the"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.51, "t": "feedback loop. These are examination favourites, but more importantly, they are"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.98, "t": "Monday-morning skills."}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.12, "t": "Why dwell on boundaries? Four reasons. Identity: you cannot offer what you cannot name;"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.61, "t": "boundaries tell a client what they are actually buying when they sit with you."}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.26, "t": "Competence: our ethical codes bind practice to training, and crossing a boundary"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.25, "t": "silently is how harm begins. Collaboration: clear roles make teamwork possible, while"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.89, "t": "blurred roles turn a case conference into a turf war. And client safety: blurred"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.03, "t": "boundaries produce duplication, contradiction and abandonment, three injuries no client"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.88, "t": "deserves. Boundaries are not walls; they are the joints that let the helping system"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.23, "t": "move."}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.43, "t": "Read the landscape row by row. Counseling psychology: postgraduate professional training"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.29, "t": "with registration through the Counsellors Registration Council of Nigeria; focus on"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 1.0, "t": "functioning, development and mild to moderate distress; methods of psychotherapy,"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.57, "t": "assessment and prevention; no prescribing. Clinical psychology: doctorate-level"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.56, "t": "training, heavier on severe psychopathology and test batteries. Psychiatry: a medical"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.77, "t": "degree plus specialization; diagnosis and pharmacotherapy; the only row that prescribes."}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.34, "t": "Social work: welfare, protection and family systems through case management and"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.54, "t": "advocacy. Psychiatric nursing: continuity of care, adherence and the therapeutic milieu."}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.75, "t": "Pastoral care: meaning, ritual and moral support under a faith community's mandate, with"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.12, "t": "no state licence. Every row saves lives the other rows cannot."}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.78, "t": "Start with our nearest neighbour, clinical psychology. We share a scientific core and"}, {"s": 0.78, "e": 0.31, "t": "much training overlap, but the centres of gravity differ. Clinical psychology leans"}, {"s": 0.31, "e": 0.1, "t": "toward severe and chronic psychopathology, an assessment-heavy culture of batteries and"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.43, "t": "differential diagnosis, hospital and forensic settings, and research on disorder"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.89, "t": "mechanisms. Counseling psychology leans toward normative life challenges alongside"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.55, "t": "disorder: study, work, love and loss; it treats strengths, functioning and vocational"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.14, "t": "behaviour as first-class data; it lives in universities, communities, workplaces and"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.87, "t": "private practice; and its research favourites are development, prevention, culture and"}, {"s": 0.87, "e": 0.07, "t": "the working alliance. Same family, different centre of gravity."}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.6, "t": "Now the medical interface. Psychiatry brings what we cannot: medical diagnosis, the"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 0.39, "t": "exclusion of organic causes, pharmacotherapy, and risk management in severe illness. We"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.25, "t": "interface through shared care: referral for medication review; counseling for adherence,"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.11, "t": "for the distress of side effects, and for adjustment to a diagnosis; and psychoeducation"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.97, "t": "for families carrying the illness home. Keep this attitude: medicine is not the enemy of"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.5, "t": "talk, and medication is not the enemy of meaning; many clients need both, sequenced"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.89, "t": "well. And avoid the classic error: counseling a client whose untreated medical or"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.42, "t": "psychotic condition makes counseling unsafe or futile. Screen first, then sit down."}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.07, "t": "Beyond the clinic sit the professions we work beside, not above. Social work holds the"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.59, "t": "system around the client: case management, welfare, housing, protection. Psychiatric"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.38, "t": "nursing holds continuity: observation, adherence, the therapeutic milieu, day after day."}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.97, "t": "School guidance holds the developmental line: guidance curricula, career information,"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.42, "t": "early identification. Rehabilitation services hold the return to work and community"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.55, "t": "roles. Pastoral care holds meaning and ritual inside communities of faith. And"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.01, "t": "traditional healing holds culturally congruent explanation and ritual, and for many"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.66, "t": "clients it is the first door, not the last. A counselor who dismisses any of these six"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.46, "t": "will lose clients to them; a counselor who understands them gains allies."}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.91, "t": "Consider pastoral care with particular care, because in our context it is often the"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.44, "t": "first resort. Its strengths are trust and access: the pulpit is frequently the first"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.02, "t": "clinic, speaking a language of meaning and hope, with continuity across the lifespan."}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.55, "t": "Its limits are real: confidentiality norms differ; some practices delay care or load"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.47, "t": "guilt onto the sufferer; and training in psychopathology varies widely. The"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.93, "t": "collaboration models that work are humble ones: consultation and respectful two-way"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.39, "t": "referral, joint psychoeducation programmes, and mental-health literacy training for"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.97, "t": "clergy who want it. Remember the client's reality: many clients want both a counselor"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.59, "t": "and a pastor. Our job is to coordinate, not to compete."}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.09, "t": "Traditional healers deserve the same seriousness. In many communities a majority of"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.59, "t": "people with mental health concerns consult a traditional or faith healer first. The"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.02, "t": "reasons are rational: cultural congruence, cost, proximity, family acceptance, and"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.66, "t": "explanations that make sense of suffering in the community's own idiom. The risks are"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.82, "t": "equally real: delayed evidence-based care, occasionally harmful practices, and"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.06, "t": "explanatory models that can override the client's own voice. Ethical engagement"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.49, "t": "therefore looks like this: respect the worldview; ask openly what has already been"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.72, "t": "tried; negotiate a plural pathway with the client's consent; and build referral"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.42, "t": "relationships with community resources before a crisis forces improvisation. The World"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.46, "t": "Health Organization's mental health gap action programme explicitly supports"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.17, "t": "task-sharing and collaboration with community resources."}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.96, "t": "Turn the landscape into practice architecture: the referral pathway in five moves. One,"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.43, "t": "screen: intake covers the presenting problem, risk, medical flags, and the client's"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.99, "t": "help-seeking path so far, including healers and pastors already involved. Two, check"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.85, "t": "competence: is this within my training, scope and current capacity? If doubtful, consult"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.64, "t": "before proceeding. Three, route: in scope means a counseling plan; medical flags mean a"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.12, "t": "physician first; severe or complex means shared care; social needs mean welfare and"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.67, "t": "social work; spiritual needs mean a pastoral link with consent. Four, warm handover:"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.46, "t": "introduce the client personally, transfer a concise summary, agree roles and consent in"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.25, "t": "writing. Five, close the loop: follow up, request feedback, document. A referral is not"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.67, "t": "complete until it is confirmed."}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.56, "t": "The ethics of moving a client between worlds reduce to five disciplines. Consent first:"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.45, "t": "explain why, to whom, and exactly what information will travel, and record the client's"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.94, "t": "decision. No abandonment: you remain responsible until the receiving professional"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.56, "t": "accepts the handover; a phone number on paper is not a referral. Minimum necessary:"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.52, "t": "share what the next professional needs, not the whole file; confidentiality survives the"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.93, "t": "referral. Know your map: be able to name your nearest psychiatrist, neurologist,"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.55, "t": "shelter, welfare office and crisis line before you need them, because crisis is the"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.51, "t": "worst time to do research. And task-sharing: in low-resource settings it is ethical only"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.71, "t": "with training, protocols and supervision, never as a shortcut."}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.4, "t": "Inside a multidisciplinary team, know your contribution and your conditions. What we"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.41, "t": "bring: strengths-based functional assessment; brief, focal, evidence-based"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.37, "t": "interventions; prevention and psychoeducation programme design; family work; and routine"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.99, "t": "outcome measurement that tells the team whether help is helping. What we ask of the"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.47, "t": "team: clear role boundaries and named responsibilities; consent-based information"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.96, "t": "sharing rather than casual corridor disclosure; respectful case conferences where"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.92, "t": "disagreement is allowed; joint review of shared clients; and protected counseling space,"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.74, "t": "because a client who cannot speak privately will not speak truthfully. Bring, and ask,"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.69, "t": "in that order."}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.67, "t": "One line to carry from this week: there is no health without mental health. That slogan,"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.45, "t": "popularised in global policy discourse from 2007, is why mental health now belongs in"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.09, "t": "primary care, in schools, in workplaces and in community programmes. It is also why"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.87, "t": "counseling psychology is an integration profession: we translate between medicine and"}, {"s": 0.87, "e": 0.58, "t": "the person, between the community and the clinic, between what a client believes and"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.36, "t": "what a client needs. Wherever health is being delivered, our competence has a seat at"}, {"s": 0.36, "e": 0.1, "t": "that table."}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.95, "t": "So carry an identity card with six entries. Strengths and development: functioning and"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.59, "t": "growth, not only symptom counts. Brief focal intervention: evidence-based help that"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.23, "t": "respects a client's time and money. Vocational expertise: career and work as mental"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.15, "t": "health variables, our historical signature since Parsons. Prevention design: programmes"}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.13, "t": "that stop harm before it starts. Multicultural competence: culture treated as a clinical"}, {"s": 0.13, "e": 0.11, "t": "fact, including our own. And outcome measurement: we measure whether help helped, and we"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.09, "t": "are willing to publish the answer. When a team forgets these contributions, remind them,"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.86, "t": "with evidence, not volume."}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.27, "t": "Gather the week. Counseling psychology sits among six helping worlds, defined by"}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.89, "t": "emphasis: functioning, development, prevention and culture. Clinical psychology and"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.57, "t": "psychiatry differ from us in centre of gravity and prescribing rights, not in worth."}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.45, "t": "Social work, nursing, school guidance, pastoral care and traditional healing are allies"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.4, "t": "with distinct mandates, and our clients often use several of them at once. Referral is a"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.95, "t": "five-move discipline: screen, check, route, warm handover, close the loop. And the"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.63, "t": "ethics hold throughout: consent, no abandonment, minimum necessary disclosure, and a"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.47, "t": "community map you built before the crisis."}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.29, "t": "Your task before week four has three parts. First, draw the referral map of your local"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.7, "t": "government area: at least one named resource in each of six categories, medical,"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.97, "t": "psychiatric, social, educational, faith-based and traditional. Second, write a"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.57, "t": "one-hundred-and-fifty-word warm referral letter for this vignette: a"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.46, "t": "twenty-nine-year-old teacher with low mood, weight loss and a morning-worse rhythm, who"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.41, "t": "is currently seeing a traditional healer. Third, interview or telephone one professional"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.16, "t": "from a neighbouring profession and ask a single question: what do you wish counselors"}, {"s": 0.16, "e": 0.7, "t": "understood about your work? Bring the answer to the seminar. Next week we open the"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.52, "t": "theories: psychodynamic, humanistic and existential foundations. See you in week four."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 742.52, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W03-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w03-captions.vtt"}, {"id": "w04", "num": 4, "title": "Theoretical Orientations I: Psychodynamic, Humanistic and Existential", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w04/01-title.png", "title": "Theoretical Orientations I", "start": 0.0, "end": 40.49}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 40.49, "end": 75.98}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/03-why-theory.png", "title": "Theory as a map, and the conceptualisation chain", "start": 75.98, "end": 122.09}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/04-family-tree.png", "title": "Six branches; three we climb this week", "start": 122.09, "end": 168.07}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/05-psychodynamic-concepts.png", "title": "Core concepts: conflict, defence, transference", "start": 168.07, "end": 211.38}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/06-psychodynamic-line.png", "title": "The psychodynamic line of work", "start": 211.38, "end": 263.45}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/07-psychodynamic-eval.png", "title": "Psychodynamic: strengths, limits, cultural fit", "start": 263.45, "end": 318.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/08-freud-quote.png", "title": "freud-quote", "start": 318.46, "end": 342.07}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/09-person-centred.png", "title": "Rogers: the conditions that carry change", "start": 342.07, "end": 396.45}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/10-pc-caricature.png", "title": "What person-centred is, and is not", "start": 396.45, "end": 440.69}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/11-gestalt.png", "title": "Gestalt: awareness, experiment, ownership", "start": 440.69, "end": 494.03}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/12-existential.png", "title": "The givens of existence and the courage to face them", "start": 494.03, "end": 544.59}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/13-four-orientations.png", "title": "Four orientations side by side", "start": 544.59, "end": 610.01}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/14-cultural-fit.png", "title": "Whose culture is inside these theories?", "start": 610.01, "end": 671.38}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 4 in review", "start": 671.38, "end": 709.07}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w04/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 709.07, "end": 756.0}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.94, "t": "Welcome to week four of CPY 701, the first of two weeks on theoretical orientations. If"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.74, "t": "weeks one to three told you who we are and where we sit, weeks four and five hand you"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.34, "t": "the lenses through which counselors see a client. Today: three great families, the"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.14, "t": "psychodynamic, the humanistic-experiential and the existential, from Freud's couch to"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.54, "t": "Rogers's chair to Frankl's search for meaning. By the end you will explain each"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.34, "t": "orientation's view of suffering, its engine of change, the counselor's stance and its"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.25, "t": "signature techniques, and you will begin your first theory-informed case"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.48, "t": "conceptualisation."}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.22, "t": "Four outcomes. One, explain the key concepts, goals and techniques of psychodynamic,"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.68, "t": "person-centred, Gestalt and existential counseling. Two, evaluate the strengths,"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.55, "t": "limitations and cultural fit of each orientation, including fit with Nigerian clients."}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.28, "t": "Three, compare their assumptions about human nature side by side. Four, produce your"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.88, "t": "first theory-informed case conceptualisation using a structured chain: data, lens,"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.82, "t": "hypothesis, intervention, evaluation. Hold on to outcome four; it is the skill that all"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.98, "t": "the others serve."}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.56, "t": "A theory is not a dogma; it is a map with a legend. It tells you what to notice, what to"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.82, "t": "ignore and what to do next, and it declares its assumptions openly. Without theory,"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.41, "t": "counseling becomes conversation with good intentions; with only one theory, it becomes a"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.61, "t": "recipe applied to people who never read the cookbook. So we aim for pluralism with"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.55, "t": "coherence: several lenses, one disciplined method. And here is the method, the"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.14, "t": "conceptualisation chain you will use with every orientation: gather data; choose a lens;"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.21, "t": "hypothesise what maintains the suffering; select the intervention the hypothesis"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.6, "t": "implies; evaluate whether help helped. Five links. Every theory we meet this week and"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 0.09, "t": "next is a different way of filling links two and three."}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.29, "t": "Picture the family tree of counseling theories as six branches. This week we climb"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.36, "t": "three. The psychodynamic branch: suffering as unconscious conflict and repeating"}, {"s": 0.36, "e": 0.94, "t": "relational patterns. The humanistic-experiential branch: suffering as blocked growth and"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.46, "t": "disowned experience. The existential branch: suffering as confrontation with the givens"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.73, "t": "of existence. Next week, three more: the behavioural-cognitive branch, suffering as"}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.12, "t": "learned and thinking patterns; the constructivist branch, suffering as story; and the"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.51, "t": "systemic branch, suffering as relationship and context. Six branches, one tree: every"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.03, "t": "branch attempts to explain how change happens. A mature counselor can name which branch"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.07, "t": "they are standing on at any moment of a session."}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.49, "t": "Begin with psychodynamic thinking. Its claims: much of mental life is unconscious;"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.1, "t": "psychic life is determined, so nothing in the mind is accidental; defences protect us"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.39, "t": "from anxiety but distort reality and consume energy; early attachment and object"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.07, "t": "relations template our adult relationships; and transference, the client replaying old"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.68, "t": "relational patterns with you, is not interference but data, perhaps the most valuable"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.16, "t": "data in the room. Countertransference, your side of the same dance, is a diagnostic"}, {"s": 0.16, "e": 0.65, "t": "instrument once examined and a hazard while unexamined. Suffering, in this lens, is"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.4, "t": "conflict: wish against fear, love against hate, loyalty against freedom."}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.01, "t": "The classical technique follows a line. Free association: say whatever comes, and the"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.23, "t": "seams will show. Dream analysis and slips: the unconscious speaks in compromise"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.78, "t": "formations, so listen for them. Interpretation of resistance: what the client avoids"}, {"s": 0.78, "e": 0.59, "t": "marks exactly where the work lives. Transference work: the old pattern repeats live with"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.34, "t": "you, and therefore can be examined live. And working through: insight repeated until it"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.95, "t": "becomes structure, not merely news. The goal is insight and structural change, making"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.97, "t": "the unconscious conscious so that the self can govern what once governed it."}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.66, "t": "Contemporary brief psychodynamic therapies compress this into twenty to forty sessions"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.27, "t": "around a core conflictual relationship theme, and that brief form is the version most"}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.45, "t": "worth knowing for practice today."}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.07, "t": "Evaluate honestly. Strengths: depth, because it explains meaning and repetition, the"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.75, "t": "patterns clients recognise but cannot stop; a genuine evidence base for brief dynamic"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.56, "t": "therapy in depression and some anxiety presentations; and a sophisticated theory of the"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.38, "t": "relationship itself. Limits: the classical form is long and costly; its concepts resist"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 1.0, "t": "measurement; and progress can be hard to demonstrate to clients, funders and courts."}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.55, "t": "Cultural assumptions: an introspective, verbal, individual self; insight as virtue;"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.89, "t": "verbal candor as health. These are cultural positions, not universal facts. With"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.58, "t": "Nigerian clients, ask before assuming: whose meaning system defines insight here, and"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.26, "t": "does the client share it? In practice, the brief psychodynamic form fits our settings"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.47, "t": "far better than classical analysis; learn the brief form first."}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.29, "t": "Freud condensed the whole project into six words: where id was, there ego shall be. Not"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.17, "t": "the elimination of desire and conflict, but the enlargement of the part of the self that"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.85, "t": "can look at them, name them and choose. Every later orientation either inherited that"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.74, "t": "ambition or rebelled against it, and the first great rebellion is our second family this"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.07, "t": "week."}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.75, "t": "Now the rebellion that became its own tradition. Rogers reversed the authority: the"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.29, "t": "client, not the expert, holds the map of their own experience. Change occurs when"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.17, "t": "certain conditions persist, and three carry the practice. Congruence: the counselor is"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.19, "t": "real and transparent within the relationship, not a mask. Unconditional positive regard:"}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.25, "t": "prizing the person without making change the price of acceptance. Empathic"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.13, "t": "understanding: sensing the client's private world as if it were your own, without ever"}, {"s": 0.13, "e": 0.15, "t": "losing the as-if. The actualising tendency does the rest: given these conditions, people"}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.69, "t": "move toward becoming. And technique here is not a set of tricks but a discipline:"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.43, "t": "reflections that test your understanding moment by moment, and the courage to remain"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.44, "t": "non-directive when every fiber urges advice."}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.39, "t": "Let us clear the caricature. Person-centred work is not permissiveness, not the absence"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.34, "t": "of method, not just listening while a client rambles. It is disciplined presence: every"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.74, "t": "reflection is a hypothesis offered for correction; every silence is chosen, not"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.63, "t": "defaulted to; and the non-directiveness is a commitment to the client's authority over"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.37, "t": "their own life, which is harder than directing. Nor is it naive: Rogers measured his"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.84, "t": "conditions, invited observation and welcomed disconfirmation. The person-centred"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.38, "t": "tradition gave our field its first rigorous process research and, eventually, the"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.69, "t": "common-factors evidence base that every orientation now shares."}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.76, "t": "Gestalt therapy radicalises presence into experiment. Its concepts: awareness as the"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.68, "t": "engine of change; the here-and-now as the only place experience exists; figure and"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.03, "t": "ground, what emerges as urgent against the background of the field; unfinished business,"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.24, "t": "unexpressed feeling that organises present contact; and contact boundaries, the styles"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.38, "t": "by which we interrupt meeting. Its techniques are experiments, not prescriptions: the"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.66, "t": "empty chair for dialogue with a person or a part; exaggeration of a gesture to hear its"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.65, "t": "message; staying with the feeling rather than talking about it; dream work as lived"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.01, "t": "scene. The goal is integration and ownership: the client moves from it happens to me, to"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.05, "t": "I do this. It demands consent, pacing and cultural care."}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.33, "t": "The existential orientation begins not from pathology but from the givens of existence:"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.4, "t": "death; freedom and its responsibility; existential isolation; and the possibility of"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.6, "t": "meaninglessness. Yalom's point: psychopathology often arises from collision with these"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 0.74, "t": "givens, so anxiety is sometimes not a symptom to remove but an accurate perception of"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.02, "t": "the human condition. The counselor's work is phenomenological and Socratic: explore how"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.8, "t": "this person lives their givens, where they flee freedom or deny limits. Frankl's"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.43, "t": "logotherapy adds the will to meaning and tragic optimism: even in unchangeable"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.5, "t": "suffering, a stance can be chosen. The goals are authenticity, responsibility, and a"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.59, "t": "meaning the client can carry."}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.61, "t": "Set the four orientations of this week side by side and the differences become crisp."}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.85, "t": "Psychodynamic: suffering as unconscious conflict; change through insight and the working"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.45, "t": "through of transference; the counselor as interpreter of the repeating pattern;"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.41, "t": "signature moves of free association and interpretation. Person-centred: suffering as"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.29, "t": "blocked growth; change through the core conditions; the counselor as real, prizing,"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.96, "t": "empathic companion; signature move of accurate reflection. Gestalt: suffering as"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.05, "t": "interrupted awareness; change through experiment in the here-and-now; the counselor as"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.65, "t": "active director of experiments; signature move of the empty chair. Existential:"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.04, "t": "suffering as collision with the givens; change through courageous facing and"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.92, "t": "meaning-making; the counselor as fellow traveller and questioner; signature move of"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.09, "t": "Socratic exploration. Each row also carries cultural assumptions; evaluate them, do not"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.01, "t": "swallow them."}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.1, "t": "Now the question week two trained you to ask: whose culture is inside these theories?"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.27, "t": "Psychodynamic thinking assumes an introspective, verbal, individual self, with insight"}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.58, "t": "as the prize. Person-centred assumptions of self-direction can collide with hierarchical"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.53, "t": "and communal expectations, yet its conditions of warmth, prizing and empathy travel"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.55, "t": "astonishingly well across cultures. Gestalt's expressive experiments meet norms that"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.29, "t": "discipline public feeling, so consent and pacing become ethical necessities, not"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.31, "t": "stylistic choices. Existentialism is framed in a secular idiom, yet its questions of"}, {"s": 0.31, "e": 0.83, "t": "meaning, death and responsibility resonate deeply with religious and communal"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.14, "t": "worldviews, including African philosophies of personhood-in-community. The standing rule"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.3, "t": "from week two holds: test imported theory locally, adapt with transparency, and report"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.38, "t": "what you learn."}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.04, "t": "Gather the week. Four orientations, four answers to the questions why does this person"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.76, "t": "suffer and how does change happen: unconscious conflict and insight; blocked growth and"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.36, "t": "the core conditions; interrupted awareness and present experiment; collision with the"}, {"s": 0.36, "e": 0.82, "t": "givens and courageous meaning-making. Each carries a stance for the counselor and a"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.48, "t": "signature technique, and each carries cultural assumptions to be evaluated rather than"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.2, "t": "swallowed. And above them all sits the chain that holds your practice together whatever"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.08, "t": "the lens: data, lens, hypothesis, intervention, evaluation."}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.48, "t": "Your task before week five. Take the week-three vignette, the twenty-nine-year-old"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.01, "t": "teacher, and write four mini-conceptualisations, one per orientation from this week:"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.4, "t": "exactly three sentences each on what maintains the suffering, what the counselor's"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.93, "t": "stance is, and what the first intervention would be. Then write one paragraph on the"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.72, "t": "orientation you personally lean toward, answering a single question: what might it blind"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.38, "t": "you to? Bring both to the seminar; the four mini-conceptualisations feed directly into"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.1, "t": "the week-nine formulation report. Next week: behavioural, cognitive, constructivist and"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.43, "t": "systemic orientations, third-wave therapies, and the common-factors evidence that"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.0, "t": "humbles them all. See you in week five."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 756.0, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W04-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w04-captions.vtt"}, {"id": "w05", "num": 5, "title": "Theoretical Orientations II: CBT, Constructivist, Systemic and Third-Wave", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w05/01-title.png", "title": "Theoretical Orientations II", "start": 0.0, "end": 47.63}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 47.63, "end": 86.57}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/03-behavioural-foundations.png", "title": "Behaviour therapy: suffering as learned pattern", "start": 86.57, "end": 138.71}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/04-exposure-line.png", "title": "Exposure and behavioural activation: the sequence every protocol shares", "start": 138.71, "end": 192.55}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/05-cognitive-beck.png", "title": "Cognitive therapy (Beck): the appraisal is the target", "start": 192.55, "end": 247.07}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/06-rebt-ellis.png", "title": "REBT (Ellis): disputing the musts", "start": 247.07, "end": 295.05}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/07-epictetus.png", "title": "epictetus", "start": 295.05, "end": 315.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/08-cbt-integrator.png", "title": "CBT: architecture, evidence, and why it travels", "start": 315.06, "end": 370.27}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/09-third-wave.png", "title": "Acceptance, mindfulness and values: changing the relationship to experience", "start": 370.27, "end": 429.21}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/10-narrative.png", "title": "Narrative therapy: the person is not the problem", "start": 429.21, "end": 487.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/11-sfbt.png", "title": "Solution-focused brief therapy: constructivism in a hurry", "start": 487.46, "end": 537.62}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/12-family-systems.png", "title": "Family systems: relocating suffering between people", "start": 537.62, "end": 585.67}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/13-six-orientations.png", "title": "This week's six orientations side by side", "start": 585.67, "end": 633.11}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/14-common-factors-culture.png", "title": "Common factors, the dodo verdict, and cultural fit", "start": 633.11, "end": 692.4}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 5 in review", "start": 692.4, "end": 730.68}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w05/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 730.68, "end": 793.61}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.99, "t": "Welcome to week five of CPY 701, the second of our two weeks on theoretical"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.39, "t": "orientations. Last week we climbed the psychodynamic, humanistic-experiential and"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.18, "t": "existential branches of the family tree. Today we complete the tree: the"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.71, "t": "behavioural-cognitive branch, where suffering is learned and thinking patterns; the"}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.17, "t": "constructivist branch, where suffering is a story that can be re-authored; and the"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.9, "t": "systemic branch, where suffering lives between people rather than inside one. We close"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.49, "t": "with the evidence that humbles every branch, the common factors. By the end you will"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.22, "t": "explain each orientation's concepts and techniques, evaluate its evidence and cultural"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.61, "t": "fit, and choose and justify a lens for a named presenting problem."}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.21, "t": "Four outcomes. One, explain the concepts, goals and techniques of behaviour therapy,"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.0, "t": "cognitive therapy and REBT, the third-wave therapies, narrative therapy,"}, {"s": 0.0, "e": 0.73, "t": "solution-focused brief therapy and family systems. Two, evaluate the evidence base and"}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.46, "t": "cultural fit of each, including fit with Nigerian clients and settings. Three, account"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.18, "t": "for the common-factors research: what actually makes therapy work across orientations."}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.91, "t": "Four, extend your case conceptualisation: choose an orientation for a named presenting"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.57, "t": "problem and justify it. Outcome four feeds your comparative essay, due in week seven."}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.88, "t": "The behavioural branch begins with a radical simplicity: do not ask what the symptom"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.41, "t": "means; ask how it was learned and what now maintains it. Classical conditioning, Pavlov"}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.8, "t": "and Watson: neutral cues paired with fear come to trigger fear. Operant conditioning,"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.11, "t": "Skinner: consequences shape behaviour, so avoidance persists because it pays. Social"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.42, "t": "learning, Bandura: we acquire patterns by watching models, and self-efficacy governs"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.95, "t": "whether we act. Wolpe added systematic desensitisation in nineteen fifty-eight, pairing"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.04, "t": "relaxation with graded exposure, and it worked measurably. Suffering is a learned"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.57, "t": "pattern maintained by its consequences; change is new learning, and the counselor is an"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.7, "t": "active trainer."}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.31, "t": "Follow the behavioural technique line, the sequence every exposure protocol shares. One,"}, {"s": 0.31, "e": 0.92, "t": "psychoeducation: name the cycle with the client, fear cue, avoidance, short-term relief,"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 1.0, "t": "long-term cost. Two, build the hierarchy: list feared situations and rank them by"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.61, "t": "expected distress. Three, expose: enter the situation, or the memory, deliberately, with"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.14, "t": "consent. Four, prevent the response: stay without escaping or neutralising, so the fear"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.68, "t": "curve falls and new learning lands. Five, consolidate: repeat until the item is boring,"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.14, "t": "climb the hierarchy, and generalise to real life. Behavioural activation runs the same"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.75, "t": "logic for depression: schedule valued activities before motivation returns, then let the"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.55, "t": "consequences rebuild it."}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.18, "t": "The cognitive turn asks a different question: not what was learned, but what the"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.95, "t": "experience means. Aaron Beck, treating depressed patients in the nineteen sixties,"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.93, "t": "noticed streams of spontaneous negative thoughts, and proposed the cognitive triad: a"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.12, "t": "negative view of self, world and future. Beneath the thoughts sit schemas, lenses fitted"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.31, "t": "in childhood that filter incoming data, and the distortions, habits of biased inference:"}, {"s": 0.31, "e": 0.01, "t": "all-or-nothing thinking, catastrophising, mind reading. Suffering here is not the"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.92, "t": "situation but the appraisal of it, and appraisals are testable. Change comes through"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.9, "t": "collaborative empiricism: every thought is a hypothesis put on trial. The techniques:"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.09, "t": "thought records, Socratic guided discovery, behavioural experiments, and schema work for"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.07, "t": "deeper layers."}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.77, "t": "Albert Ellis arrived earlier, in nineteen fifty-five, with a more confrontational"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.33, "t": "cousin: rational emotive behaviour therapy. Its engine is the ABC model. A, the"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.95, "t": "activating event: what happened. B, the beliefs, and here is the pivot: rational"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.08, "t": "preferences versus irrational demands framed as musts, I must perform well, others must"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.27, "t": "treat me fairly, life must be comfortable. C, the consequences, which follow from B, not"}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.46, "t": "from A. Then D, disputation: the counselor actively challenges the demands, where is the"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.58, "t": "evidence that you must be approved? And E, a new effective philosophy and its emotions."}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.92, "t": "The tone is direct, disputational, often humorous; the goal is unconditional"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.05, "t": "self-acceptance."}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.84, "t": "Ellis borrowed his motto from the Stoic philosopher Epictetus: men are not disturbed by"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.62, "t": "things, but by the views which they take of them. Two thousand years old, and still the"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.08, "t": "cleanest one-sentence statement of the cognitive branch: between event and emotion"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.07, "t": "stands a belief, and beliefs can be examined."}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.92, "t": "Behaviour and cognition merged into CBT, now the most researched family of treatments in"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.77, "t": "the world. Its architecture: a structured session agenda; problems defined concretely; a"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.23, "t": "shared formulation drawn with the client, not delivered at them; skills taught and"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.75, "t": "practised; homework, because change happens in the week, not the hour; and outcomes"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.47, "t": "measured. It is time-limited by design, twelve to twenty sessions, and transdiagnostic"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.25, "t": "protocols treat whole clusters, worry, rumination, avoidance, through shared processes."}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.97, "t": "For Nigerian practice this matters twice: the largest evidence base to point at, and a"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.63, "t": "structured, psychoeducational style that travels well in clinics, schools and digital"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.48, "t": "formats. Its limits: it presumes verbal articulacy, can underweight meaning, culture and"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.27, "t": "relationship, and homework assumes a stable life context."}, {"s": 0.27, "e": 0.84, "t": "The third wave keeps the empiricism and questions the machinery. Mindfulness-based"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.88, "t": "approaches: Kabat-Zinn's stress reduction since nineteen seventy-nine, and"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.86, "t": "mindfulness-based cognitive therapy, built to stop relapse in depression by changing the"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.57, "t": "relationship to thoughts, watching them as events rather than truths. Acceptance and"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.94, "t": "Commitment Therapy, Hayes: the target is psychological flexibility, not symptom"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.85, "t": "reduction; six processes, accepting, defusing, present-moment contact, self-as-context,"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.77, "t": "values, and committed action. Dialectical Behaviour Therapy, Linehan: built for chronic"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.0, "t": "suicidality and emotion dysregulation, on a biosocial theory, an invalidating"}, {"s": 0.0, "e": 0.37, "t": "environment meeting a sensitive temperament, with four skills modules held in a"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.88, "t": "dialectic of acceptance and change. All three say the same deep thing: change the"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.21, "t": "relationship to experience, not only its content."}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.71, "t": "The constructivist branch starts elsewhere entirely: people live by stories, and"}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.49, "t": "problems colonise the plots. Michael White and David Epston shaped narrative therapy"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.71, "t": "around a refusal: the person is not the problem; the problem is the problem."}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.77, "t": "Externalisation gives the problem a character and a name, so a child does not have anger"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.68, "t": "but faces The Temper, and the relationship to it can change. Then comes the search for"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.25, "t": "unique outcomes: moments the dominant story missed, when the problem did not win."}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.17, "t": "Re-authoring weaves those exceptions into a preferred plot, and therapeutic documents,"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.08, "t": "letters and certificates, put the new story in writing and in community. The stance is"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.86, "t": "decentred and influential: the counselor is an editor and co-investigator, never the"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.7, "t": "author of the client's life. Suffering is a saturated story; change is re-membering a"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.46, "t": "richer one."}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.44, "t": "Solution-focused brief therapy, de Shazer and Berg in Milwaukee, is constructivism in a"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.42, "t": "hurry, and its brevity is its argument. It barely examines the problem; it searches for"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.4, "t": "the solution already flickering. The miracle question: suppose tonight a miracle solves"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.1, "t": "this problem, what is the first small sign tomorrow morning that life is different?"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.81, "t": "Scaling questions: where are you from zero to ten, and what moved you one point up?"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.72, "t": "Exception questions: when was the problem smaller, and what was different then? Coping"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.21, "t": "questions carry the hardest weeks. Therapy averages three to eight sessions. For"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.06, "t": "Nigerian settings: high need, few specialists, and cultural fluency in hope language."}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.63, "t": "Brief is not shallow; it is economics made clinical."}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.47, "t": "The systemic branch relocates suffering from inside the person to between people. The"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.24, "t": "lens: circularity, behaviour is both cause and effect in loops; homeostasis, systems"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.67, "t": "resist change, and one member's improvement can upset the balance of the whole;"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.65, "t": "boundaries and subsystems, Minuchin mapped enmeshment and disengagement; and triangles,"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.49, "t": "Bowen showed how dyads under stress recruit a third, and made differentiation of self"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.54, "t": "the goal. The practice: genograms chart multigenerational patterns; enactments bring the"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.45, "t": "fight into the room and restructure it live; and the identified patient is reframed as"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.09, "t": "the family's symptom-bearer. Suffering is a pattern of the system; change is a new"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.67, "t": "pattern of interaction."}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.8, "t": "Behaviour therapy: learned patterns; new learning through exposure; the counselor as"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.15, "t": "trainer. CBT: distorted appraisals; collaborative testing of thoughts; the counselor as"}, {"s": 0.15, "e": 0.58, "t": "co-scientist. Third wave: entanglement and struggle; acceptance, mindfulness and values;"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.0, "t": "the counselor as coach of flexibility. Narrative: a saturated story; re-authoring around"}, {"s": 0.0, "e": 0.35, "t": "unique outcomes; the counselor as decentred editor. Solution-focused: problem-saturated"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.41, "t": "talk; solution-building from exceptions; the counselor as questioner of exceptions."}, {"s": 0.41, "e": 0.76, "t": "Family systems: relational patterns; new interactions; the counselor as director of the"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.12, "t": "system. Six rows, one question: which pattern?"}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.74, "t": "Now the humbling evidence. Rosenzweig named the dodo bird verdict in nineteen"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.02, "t": "thirty-six: everybody has won, and all must have prizes. Lambert's analysis put shares"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.08, "t": "on it: roughly forty per cent of improvement comes from client strengths and events"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.21, "t": "outside therapy, thirty from the relationship, fifteen from hope and expectancy, and"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.42, "t": "only about fifteen from the model and technique. So orientations are not rival truths"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.11, "t": "but structured ways of delivering the same ingredients: a rationale, a healing"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.32, "t": "relationship, expectancy, and practice. Cultural fit: CBT suits structured brief care"}, {"s": 0.32, "e": 0.52, "t": "and schools; narrative and solution-focused work speak the language of proverbs, hope"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.44, "t": "and community; family therapy must treat the extended family as a resource, not a"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.4, "t": "pathology. Interdependence is not enmeshment until proven otherwise."}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.65, "t": "Gather the week. Six orientations added to the tree: behaviour, cognition, their merger"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.83, "t": "into CBT, the third wave, narrative re-authoring, solution-focused brevity, and family"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.5, "t": "systems. Each names a different pattern to treat: learned behaviour, appraisal,"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.54, "t": "entanglement, story, talk, relationship. The common factors bind them: relationship,"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.5, "t": "expectancy, rationale and practice do most of the work. And your chain holds: data,"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.46, "t": "lens, hypothesis, intervention, evaluation, now with nine lenses to choose from and"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.69, "t": "evidence to justify the choice."}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.5, "t": "Your task before week six, and it is assessed. Write a comparative essay of about"}, {"s": 0.5, "e": 0.68, "t": "fifteen hundred words: choose one presenting problem common in Nigerian practice, exam"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.93, "t": "anxiety, depression in students, marital distress, grief, and argue for one orientation"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.11, "t": "from weeks four or five. Include a conceptualisation using the chain; three techniques"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.21, "t": "with what each targets; an honest cultural-fit critique; and at least two Nigerian or"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.46, "t": "African empirical references. Submit in week seven; it is your seminar paper. Second, a"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.64, "t": "ten-minute rehearsal: try one technique on a willing peer, a thought record, a scaling"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.75, "t": "question, an externalising conversation. Do not therapise them; rehearse the move and"}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 1.0, "t": "write process notes on what was hard. Bring the notes to week six, where theory becomes"}, {"s": 1.0, "e": 0.89, "t": "skill: the counseling process, the microskills laboratory, and your first recorded"}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.61, "t": "practice. See you there."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 793.61, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W05-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w05-captions.vtt"}, {"id": "w06", "num": 6, "title": "The Counseling Process and Core Microskills", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w06/01-title.png", "title": "The Counseling Process and Microskills", "start": 0.0, "end": 49.74}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 49.74, "end": 95.02}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/03-process-stages.png", "title": "The counseling process in five stages", "start": 95.02, "end": 147.18}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/04-first-session.png", "title": "Anatomy of the first session", "start": 147.18, "end": 193.64}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/05-attending.png", "title": "Attending behaviour: the skill underneath every skill", "start": 193.64, "end": 246.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/06-listening.png", "title": "Active listening: encouragers, paraphrase, reflection of feeling", "start": 246.06, "end": 298.26}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/07-deeply-heard.png", "title": "deeply-heard", "start": 298.26, "end": 314.15}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/08-questioning.png", "title": "Questioning: the scalpel, not the hammer", "start": 314.15, "end": 364.28}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/09-high-voltage.png", "title": "Silence, tears and other high-voltage moments", "start": 364.28, "end": 420.77}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/10-summarising.png", "title": "Summarising, structuring and pacing", "start": 420.77, "end": 468.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/11-influencing.png", "title": "The influencing skills: immediacy, challenge, disclosure", "start": 468.06, "end": 512.63}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/12-hierarchy.png", "title": "The microskills hierarchy in three levels", "start": 512.63, "end": 561.76}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/13-pitfalls.png", "title": "Six beginner pitfalls and their corrections", "start": 561.76, "end": 612.49}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/14-nigerian-calibration.png", "title": "Microskills, Nigerian edition", "start": 612.49, "end": 664.82}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 6 in review", "start": 664.82, "end": 702.06}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w06/16-task.png", "title": "Applied task and next week", "start": 702.06, "end": 765.24}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.03, "t": "Welcome to week six of CPY 701, where theory becomes practice. Weeks four and five gave"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.98, "t": "you nine lenses for seeing suffering; this week gives you the hands. Every orientation"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.38, "t": "we studied is delivered through the same medium: a conversation conducted with"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.72, "t": "disciplined skill. Today we walk the counseling process from first contact to"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.81, "t": "termination, and then we drill the microskills, the smallest units of that conversation,"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.77, "t": "the way a musician drills scales. By the end you will structure the process across its"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.52, "t": "stages, run a first session, demonstrate the core listening and influencing skills,"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.4, "t": "recognise and correct beginner pitfalls, and adapt every skill to Nigerian relational"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.73, "t": "norms. This week opens your practice laboratory."}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.99, "t": "Four outcomes. One, structure the counseling process across its stages, from"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.88, "t": "relationship building through assessment, intervention and evaluation, to termination"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.83, "t": "and follow-up. Two, demonstrate the core microskills: attending, listening, reflection"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.51, "t": "of feeling, questioning and summarising, plus the influencing skills of immediacy,"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.4, "t": "confrontation and self-disclosure. Three, diagnose common beginner pitfalls and apply"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.35, "t": "deliberate corrections. Four, adapt every skill to Nigerian relational norms: respect,"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.96, "t": "eye contact, indirectness, gender and age dynamics. Outcome two is assessed: your"}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.02, "t": "recorded microskills demonstration counts for ten per cent of the course."}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.98, "t": "The process has an arc, and the arc holds whatever lens you use. Stage one, relationship"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.74, "t": "building: safety before strategy; rapport, consent and confidentiality settled early,"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.29, "t": "because the alliance is the strongest common factor under your control. Stage two,"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.18, "t": "assessment and goals: gather the story and the strengths, screen risk, and set goals in"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.94, "t": "the client's own language, concrete enough to measure. Stage three, intervention: the"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.9, "t": "working phase, your chosen lens in action, techniques paced to the alliance. Stage four,"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.86, "t": "evaluation: routine outcome monitoring, asking whether help is helping, and adjusting on"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.62, "t": "evidence. Stage five, termination and follow-up: end deliberately, review gains, plan"}, {"s": 0.62, "e": 0.17, "t": "for setbacks, say goodbye properly, and schedule the contact that closes the loop."}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.86, "t": "Zoom into stage one: the anatomy of a first session. The opening five minutes matter"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.82, "t": "more than they look: greet, seat, water; state your role and what happens today. Consent"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.65, "t": "and confidentiality come next in plain language, including the limits; record it. Then"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.61, "t": "the invitation: what brings you here? Listen long: the first telling carries the content"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.57, "t": "and the client's test of you. Screen as you listen: risk, medical flags, substances, and"}, {"s": 0.57, "e": 0.26, "t": "supports; week three's discipline, screen before you sit down. Close with structure:"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.95, "t": "summarise what you heard in the client's own words, agree one next step and the next"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.64, "t": "meeting. Then document the same day: the record serves care, ethics and supervision."}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.55, "t": "Microskills stack in levels, and level one is attending: the skill underneath every"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.46, "t": "skill. Egan's SOLER gives the body a syntax: face the client squarely, keep an open"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.66, "t": "posture, lean in slightly, hold culturally apt eye contact, and stay relaxed. The vocal"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.85, "t": "channel matters as much: let tone and pace follow the client's affect; your voice is an"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.05, "t": "instrument, not a metronome. Verbally, follow the client's topics and key words; do not"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.1, "t": "import your own agenda early. And attune culturally: eye-contact norms differ by age,"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.09, "t": "gender and status, and in many Nigerian settings a lowered gaze signals respect, not"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.21, "t": "evasion, so calibrate SOLER to the person, not the textbook. Attending is the delivery"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.06, "t": "system for all that follows; unskilled presence leaks."}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.32, "t": "Level two is active listening, and it has three instruments. Minimal encouragers: mm, go"}, {"s": 0.32, "e": 0.52, "t": "on, a nod, low-cost signals that keep the story moving without steering it. Paraphrase:"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.72, "t": "return the content in fewer words and check it. Reflection of feeling: name the emotion"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.98, "t": "behind the content, you sound angry, and underneath that, hurt. The formula is a feeling"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.97, "t": "word plus its context, offered tentatively and corrected without shame. The accuracy"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.95, "t": "test: a good reflection earns a yes, a deepening, or a correction, and all three are"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.07, "t": "progress, because each tells you the client felt heard enough to go further or set you"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.98, "t": "right. A deflection or a change of subject usually means you missed. Missing is not"}, {"s": 0.98, "e": 0.26, "t": "failure; failing to notice that you missed is."}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.69, "t": "Rogers captured what level two is for: when a person realises he has been deeply heard,"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.07, "t": "his eyes moisten, as though he is saying, thank God, somebody heard me. In most of our"}, {"s": 0.07, "e": 0.19, "t": "clients' lives, that experience is rarer than advice, and far more transformative."}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.37, "t": "Questioning is the scalpel of listening, and like a scalpel it cuts both ways. Open"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.74, "t": "questions, what was that like, invite narrative; use them to explore. Closed questions"}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.24, "t": "invite one-word answers; use them for facts and risk screening, where precision matters,"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.55, "t": "not for conversation. Beware the why trap: why did you stay sounds like an accusation"}, {"s": 0.55, "e": 0.8, "t": "even when it is not meant as one; recast it, what made staying possible, or what did"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.85, "t": "staying do for you. Watch your question density: two questions in a row without a"}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.23, "t": "reflection in between flips the session into interrogation, and the client becomes the"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.54, "t": "witness rather than the author. The reliable sequence is listen, reflect, then ask: a"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.03, "t": "question that follows a reflection lands on softened ground, and the client answers from"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.28, "t": "experience rather than from defence."}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.32, "t": "Some moments carry more voltage than words. Silence is a skill: count slowly, because"}, {"s": 0.32, "e": 0.28, "t": "the client's silence is usually work, not breakdown; interrupting steals the insight"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.32, "t": "forming inside it. If silence hardens into shutdown, name it gently: I notice we went"}, {"s": 0.32, "e": 0.36, "t": "quiet, would it help to say what is happening? Tears: do not rush to stop them; offer"}, {"s": 0.36, "e": 0.33, "t": "tissue, presence and time; tears are data and discharge, not emergency. Anger in the"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.22, "t": "room: stay steady, do not match it or moralise it; reflect what is underneath. Risk"}, {"s": 0.22, "e": 0.76, "t": "disclosures change the register deliberately: move to direct, closed screening"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.94, "t": "questions, because a clear question about suicide does not plant the idea; it opens the"}, {"s": 0.94, "e": 0.19, "t": "door to help. And when your own emotions surge, notice, breathe, keep attending; process"}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.75, "t": "it in supervision, never in session."}, {"s": 0.75, "e": 0.58, "t": "Upper level two: summarising, structuring and pacing. Summarising bundles content,"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.76, "t": "feeling and themes at transitions and session ends; it gives clients the shape of their"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.79, "t": "own story. Structuring says out loud what a phase is for. Pacing matches the client's"}, {"s": 0.79, "e": 0.83, "t": "tempo before leading it, because deep material entered too fast produces retreat, not"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.08, "t": "progress. Notice what these moves add up to: Bordin's working alliance, bonds, goals and"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.05, "t": "tasks, is built out of exactly these behaviours, session after session. And when you"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.95, "t": "misread or miss, as you will, repair it plainly: I got that wrong, tell me again. A"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.06, "t": "repaired rupture strengthens the alliance more than smoothness ever did."}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.85, "t": "Level three is influencing: the skills that add the counselor's perspective to the room."}, {"s": 0.85, "e": 0.37, "t": "They work only on top of solid attending and listening; influence without rapport is"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.03, "t": "noise. Immediacy uses the here-and-now of this relationship: right now, as you tell me"}, {"s": 0.03, "e": 0.81, "t": "this, I notice you are smiling, what is happening between us? Supportive challenge holds"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.4, "t": "two data points side by side: you say it does not matter, and your fists say it does."}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.86, "t": "Self-disclosure must be brief, purposeful and for the client's benefit; the test is"}, {"s": 0.86, "e": 0.45, "t": "whose need it serves. And interpretation and advice are the riskiest moves: both land"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.64, "t": "only where the alliance can carry them, and both are earned, never opened with."}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.36, "t": "Ivey's intentional interviewing organises this into a hierarchy that is the curriculum."}, {"s": 0.36, "e": 0.95, "t": "Level one, attending: SOLER, vocal tone, verbal following; the body speaks before the"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.28, "t": "mouth does. Level two, listening: encouragers, paraphrase, reflection of feeling,"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.06, "t": "questioning and summarising; the client's story returns to them organised and heard, and"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.78, "t": "most of most sessions should live here. Level three, influencing: immediacy, supportive"}, {"s": 0.78, "e": 0.37, "t": "challenge, self-disclosure, interpretation and direction; the counselor's perspective"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.9, "t": "enters, dosed to what the alliance can carry. Intentional interviewing means knowing"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.68, "t": "which level you are on, why you chose it, and what the alternatives were. That awareness"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.76, "t": "separates a professional conversation from a well-meaning one."}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.93, "t": "Supervision sees six pitfalls in every cohort. Reassurance rush: don't worry, it will be"}, {"s": 0.93, "e": 0.69, "t": "fine, feels like dismissal; reflect first. Interrogation mode: closed questions in"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.44, "t": "volleys make the client a witness; listen, reflect, then one open question. Advice"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.33, "t": "early: if I were you robs the client of ownership; explore options, let them choose."}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.81, "t": "Story hijack: that happened to me too changes the session's owner; one line of"}, {"s": 0.81, "e": 0.77, "t": "disclosure, then back to them. Feeling avoidance: skipping past tears leaves the core"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.45, "t": "material unspoken; stay with that a moment. Premature depth: excavating trauma in"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.48, "t": "session two produces retreat or re-traumatisation; stabilise first. Every pitfall is a"}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.48, "t": "skill at the wrong time; the correction is another skill."}, {"s": 0.48, "e": 0.52, "t": "Now calibrate every skill to home ground. Respect grammar first: honorifics, greetings"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.34, "t": "and inquiries about family are the entry permit to the real conversation, not small"}, {"s": 0.34, "e": 0.02, "t": "talk. Eye contact: calibrate by age, gender and status; a lowered gaze may signal"}, {"s": 0.02, "e": 0.06, "t": "respect, not evasion. Indirectness: serious material often arrives wrapped in proverb,"}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.16, "t": "story or the third person; unwrap it with the client, never against them. When a parent"}, {"s": 0.16, "e": 0.19, "t": "or pastor sits in, negotiate confidentiality and private time. Gender: offer choice of"}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.3, "t": "counselor where possible; mirror conservatively until the client sets the tone. And the"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.05, "t": "communal self: goals phrased only as individual autonomy may miss their world. The"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.82, "t": "skills are universal; their expression is local; that is competence."}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.96, "t": "Gather the week. The process has five stages, and the arc holds whatever lens you bring."}, {"s": 0.96, "e": 0.6, "t": "Microskills stack in three levels, attending, listening, influencing; intentional"}, {"s": 0.6, "e": 0.53, "t": "interviewing means knowing your level and your reasons. Reflection, pacing and repair"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.67, "t": "build the alliance, the strongest common factor under your control. The six pitfalls are"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.18, "t": "each corrected by another skill, deliberately timed. Every skill needs Nigerian"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.18, "t": "calibration: respect, eye contact, indirectness, elders, gender and the communal self."}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.06, "t": "The hands are learning now."}, {"s": 0.06, "e": 0.13, "t": "Your tasks before week seven, and the second is assessed. First, form a practice triad:"}, {"s": 0.13, "e": 0.26, "t": "counselor, client, observer, and rotate. Rehearse each level separately: five minutes of"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.33, "t": "attending only, then listening, then one dosed influencing move; the observer gives one"}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.47, "t": "strength and one correction per round. Second, record a ten-minute role-play with a peer"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.39, "t": "using the week-three teacher vignette. Demonstrate five things: steady attending, two"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.46, "t": "reflections of feeling, one open question, one summary, and one repaired rupture, where"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.83, "t": "you misread something and fix it openly. Submit the recording with a one-page"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.83, "t": "self-critique in week seven; it is your microskills demonstration, worth ten per cent."}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.9, "t": "Third, one journal entry on the skill that felt hardest, and why. Next week we take the"}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.82, "t": "relationship itself as the subject: the working alliance, diversity and multicultural"}, {"s": 0.82, "e": 0.24, "t": "competence, and power in the room. See you there."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 765.24, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W06-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w06-captions.vtt"}, {"id": "w07", "num": 7, "title": "The Counseling Relationship, Diversity and Multicultural Counseling", "slides": [{"file": "/dist/slides/w07/01-title.png", "title": "The Counseling Relationship", "start": 0.0, "end": 43.72}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/02-outcomes.png", "title": "What you will be able to do by the end of this week", "start": 43.72, "end": 83.74}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/03-evidence.png", "title": "What the research actually says", "start": 83.74, "end": 133.54}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/04-bordin.png", "title": "Bordin's pan-theoretical alliance: bonds, goals, tasks", "start": 133.54, "end": 179.79}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/05-rupture-repair.png", "title": "Rupture and repair: the cycle that strengthens the alliance", "start": 179.79, "end": 239.82}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/06-empathy.png", "title": "Empathy: trainable, measurable, culturally accented", "start": 239.82, "end": 298.33}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/07-yalom.png", "title": "yalom", "start": 298.33, "end": 312.46}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/08-other-elements.png", "title": "Regard, congruence, expectation, countertransference", "start": 312.46, "end": 365.39}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/09-diversity.png", "title": "Diversity and intersectionality in the Nigerian room", "start": 365.39, "end": 413.64}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/10-frameworks.png", "title": "Multicultural competence: the frameworks", "start": 413.64, "end": 464.73}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/11-skills-audit.png", "title": "Audit the skills: every universal has an accent", "start": 464.73, "end": 514.64}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/12-power.png", "title": "Power in the room, and advocacy beyond it", "start": 514.64, "end": 565.51}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/13-differences-table.png", "title": "Six dimensions of difference: assumption, risk, grounded practice", "start": 565.51, "end": 620.89}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/14-nigerian-alliance.png", "title": "The alliance in Nigerian conditions", "start": 620.89, "end": 673.92}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/15-summary.png", "title": "Week 7 in review", "start": 673.92, "end": 712.68}, {"file": "/dist/slides/w07/16-task.png", "title": "Applied tasks and test preparation", "start": 712.68, "end": 772.46}], "cues": [{"s": 0.0, "e": 0.69, "t": "Welcome to week seven of CPY 701. Weeks four, five and six gave you lenses and hands;"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.04, "t": "this week examines the medium both float in: the counseling relationship itself."}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.72, "t": "Everything you have learned arrives through a human relationship, and the evidence is"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.61, "t": "blunt: the relationship is not a warm-up to the intervention; in substantial part, it is"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.29, "t": "the intervention. Today we build the working alliance deliberately, repair it when it"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.18, "t": "breaks, widen the frame to diversity, multicultural competence and power, and close with"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.4, "t": "what all of it means in Nigerian practice. This week also prepares you for the"}, {"s": 0.4, "e": 0.74, "t": "mid-semester test in week eight, which covers weeks one to seven."}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.49, "t": "Four outcomes. One, explain Bordin's pan-theoretical working alliance and the evidence"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.11, "t": "that the relationship contributes to outcome independently of method. Two, build and"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.53, "t": "repair the alliance deliberately: recognise rupture, metacommunicate, and use the"}, {"s": 0.53, "e": 0.01, "t": "empirically supported relationship elements. Three, apply multicultural competence"}, {"s": 0.01, "e": 0.7, "t": "frameworks, awareness, knowledge and skills, including the ADDRESSING model of social"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.39, "t": "identities. Four, analyse power and intersectionality in the room and in society, and"}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.67, "t": "practise advocacy as part of counseling. Your tasks this week also prepare your"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.74, "t": "week-eight test."}, {"s": 0.74, "e": 0.05, "t": "Start with the evidence; it changes priorities. Norcross and Lambert's consensus"}, {"s": 0.05, "e": 0.69, "t": "statement is blunt: the psychotherapy relationship makes a substantial and consistent"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.79, "t": "contribution to outcome, independent of the specific method used. Fl\u00fcckiger's"}, {"s": 0.79, "e": 0.43, "t": "meta-analysis puts the alliance-outcome correlation at roughly point two eight, among"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.8, "t": "the most robust findings in the field. Empathy, regard, genuineness, the alliance"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.04, "t": "itself, rupture repair, expectations and countertransference management are the"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.88, "t": "supported elements. This does not say technique does not matter: technique carries about"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.72, "t": "fifteen per cent of outcome and makes hope concrete. Whatever lens you hold, you deliver"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.56, "t": "it through a relationship whose quality is measurable, trainable, and ethically serious."}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.26, "t": "Bordin made the alliance pan-theoretical with three interlocking parts, and this triad"}, {"s": 0.26, "e": 0.77, "t": "is the most useful working model you will own. Bonds: the affective glue, do I feel"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.47, "t": "safe, respected and understood here? Goals: agreement on what this work is for, stated"}, {"s": 0.47, "e": 0.24, "t": "in language the client owns. Tasks: agreement on how we get there, what each of us does"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.28, "t": "in session and between sessions. Weakness in any part strains the whole, and"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.99, "t": "misalignment of goals is the commonest silent killer, because counselor and client can"}, {"s": 0.99, "e": 0.49, "t": "work hard at different projects for months without noticing. And the model travels:"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.8, "t": "psychodynamic, CBT, narrative, systemic work can all be described, monitored and"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.79, "t": "repaired in this one language."}, {"s": 0.79, "e": 0.89, "t": "Rupture is not failure; unrepaired rupture is. Safran and Muran's cycle gives the shape."}, {"s": 0.89, "e": 0.35, "t": "One, strain appears: the client withdraws, goes flat, deflects, or confronts and"}, {"s": 0.35, "e": 0.21, "t": "criticises the process. Two, notice: your body is the first instrument: tightening, a"}, {"s": 0.21, "e": 0.23, "t": "drop in warmth, a rehearsed defence. Three, name it gently, inviting exploration rather"}, {"s": 0.23, "e": 0.76, "t": "than defending. Four, metacommunicate: talk about the talking, what just happened"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.38, "t": "between us? Own your contribution without collapsing into apology; repair requires"}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.08, "t": "honesty. Five, renegotiate goals or tasks where the rupture is about direction. The"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.18, "t": "outcome: an alliance strengthened by being tested, and a client who learns that conflict"}, {"s": 0.18, "e": 0.83, "t": "with you is survivable, for many clients the deepest therapy on offer."}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.8, "t": "Now empathy itself. Empathy is not sympathy, I feel sorry for you, and not"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.66, "t": "identification, I have lived your story. It is accurate understanding of the client's"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.43, "t": "inner frame of reference, communicated so the client recognises it. Carkhuff's scale"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.97, "t": "made it trainable: level one misses the feeling; level three captures content and"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.83, "t": "feeling; level five adds the depth the client senses but has not named. Aim at three,"}, {"s": 0.83, "e": 0.77, "t": "reach for five. Week six's reflection of feeling is its instrument; a yes, a deepening"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.71, "t": "or a correction all count as progress. Empathy has a cultural syntax: in many Nigerian"}, {"s": 0.71, "e": 0.65, "t": "contexts it is carried less by feeling words than by presence, proverb, practical help"}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.33, "t": "and respectful silence. Read the idiom; keep the function."}, {"s": 0.33, "e": 0.88, "t": "Yalom carried the whole week on his personal seal: it is the relationship that heals,"}, {"s": 0.88, "e": 0.29, "t": "repeated three times, not because he lacked vocabulary, but because every school of"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.49, "t": "therapy keeps forgetting it and must be reminded."}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.77, "t": "The other classical conditions. Unconditional positive regard: acceptance without"}, {"s": 0.77, "e": 0.51, "t": "conditions of worth, prizing the person even while rejecting some behaviour; an attitude"}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.92, "t": "with behaviours, warmth of voice, patience with repetition, and no flinching at the"}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.14, "t": "shameful parts. Congruence: the counselor is real within the relationship; inner"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.69, "t": "experience matches outer expression, within what serves the client. Norcross adds two"}, {"s": 0.69, "e": 0.43, "t": "more supported elements: cultivating positive expectations through a credible rationale,"}, {"s": 0.43, "e": 0.45, "t": "because hope is an active ingredient, not a placebo to tolerate; and managing"}, {"s": 0.45, "e": 0.87, "t": "countertransference, week four's instrument, monitored and supervised, used as data"}, {"s": 0.87, "e": 0.28, "t": "rather than leaked as behaviour. Five elements, one sentence: be real, be for them,"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.39, "t": "understand them, repair what breaks, and adapt to who they are."}, {"s": 0.39, "e": 0.46, "t": "Now widen the frame. Nigeria is not one culture: more than two hundred and fifty ethnic"}, {"s": 0.46, "e": 0.54, "t": "groups, Hausa, Yoruba and Igbo among the largest; a near-even Christian-Muslim presence"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.61, "t": "with indigenous traditions woven through both; class and education gaps wider than many"}, {"s": 0.61, "e": 0.68, "t": "borders; and Nigerian Pidgin as the room's true lingua franca. Layer on gender and age,"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.76, "t": "disability, orientation, and displaced populations. Crenshaw's intersectionality is the"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.76, "t": "analytic tool: a client is not a list of categories but a crossing point where systems"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.49, "t": "of advantage and disadvantage meet, and the same identity can be oppression in one"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.0, "t": "context and strength in another. Competence begins with the honest inventory of"}, {"s": 0.0, "e": 0.63, "t": "yourself."}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.28, "t": "Competence has structure. Sue and Sue's triad: awareness of your own assumptions;"}, {"s": 0.28, "e": 0.8, "t": "knowledge of the client's worldview and its literature; and skills to intervene"}, {"s": 0.8, "e": 0.66, "t": "congruently, including knowing when to consult. Hays's ADDRESSING gives the identity"}, {"s": 0.66, "e": 0.04, "t": "checklist: Age, Disability, Religion, Ethnicity, Socioeconomic status, Sexual"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.11, "t": "orientation, Indigenous heritage, National origin, Gender. Map yourself and your client"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.91, "t": "on all nine axes, and note where power flows toward you. The APA Guidelines and ACA"}, {"s": 0.91, "e": 0.56, "t": "competencies add the standards: lifelong self-examination, attention to power and"}, {"s": 0.56, "e": 0.7, "t": "privilege, culturally sensitive assessment, and advocacy at client, community and public"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.73, "t": "levels. Competence is not a certificate; it is a posture with practices."}, {"s": 0.73, "e": 0.7, "t": "Audit the skills: every universal has a cultural accent. Direct eye contact: respect or"}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.2, "t": "defiance, depending on age and gender. Self-disclosure of feeling: liberation or"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.17, "t": "embarrassment, depending on family norms. The question, what do you want: routine in an"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.14, "t": "individualist frame, near-impossible where the self is defined through family. Silence,"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.84, "t": "touch, seating, even the clock are cultural artefacts. The discipline from week two"}, {"s": 0.84, "e": 0.54, "t": "governs: imported tools are hypotheses, not truths. Test them, adapt transparently,"}, {"s": 0.54, "e": 0.17, "t": "document what works here, and never let adaptation harden into stereotype, because"}, {"s": 0.17, "e": 0.14, "t": "culture describes contexts, never a particular person. The standing question is gentle:"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.64, "t": "how does your family talk about problems like this?"}, {"s": 0.64, "e": 0.68, "t": "Power sits in the room whether or not you name it. You hold expert power, the diagnostic"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.58, "t": "label, gatekeeping over reports, and often class and education power. Unexamined, that"}, {"s": 0.58, "e": 0.49, "t": "gradient quietly decides who speaks, which goals count as realistic, and which stories"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.19, "t": "get pathologised. The answer is to practise against it: share formulation and notes"}, {"s": 0.19, "e": 0.09, "t": "where feasible, offer choice of methods, name your limits openly, and let the client's"}, {"s": 0.09, "e": 0.79, "t": "expertise on their life outrank yours on lives in general. Beyond the room, the ACA"}, {"s": 0.79, "e": 0.49, "t": "advocacy competencies make social justice part of the job at three levels: with the"}, {"s": 0.49, "e": 0.25, "t": "client, in the community, and at systems and policy. Some suffering is manufactured;"}, {"s": 0.25, "e": 0.51, "t": "empathy alone ratifies it, and week one's advocate answers it."}, {"s": 0.51, "e": 0.37, "t": "Six dimensions to carry into practice. Age: youth is not immaturity, age is not"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.67, "t": "rigidity; adapt pace and idiom, honouring hierarchy without surrendering the client's"}, {"s": 0.67, "e": 0.68, "t": "voice. Gender: the risk is therapy reinforcing the norms producing the suffering;"}, {"s": 0.68, "e": 0.2, "t": "explore what gender costs and permits for this client. Religion: faith is neither denial"}, {"s": 0.2, "e": 0.65, "t": "nor a substitute for care; treat it as resource and stressor; clergy only with consent."}, {"s": 0.65, "e": 0.44, "t": "Ethnicity and language: shared nationality is not shared meaning; work through"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.59, "t": "interpreters and mother-tongue affect. Class and education: insight needs no formal"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.04, "t": "education; use proverbial, oral, concrete forms of the same skills. Disability: neither"}, {"s": 0.04, "e": 0.9, "t": "incapacity nor inspiration; accessibility first, then the person's own account."}, {"s": 0.9, "e": 0.76, "t": "Finally, the alliance at home. Religion is often the client's first language of"}, {"s": 0.76, "e": 0.14, "t": "suffering and hope; know when a pastor or imam is an ally and when referral is needed."}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.59, "t": "Family: in many settings the real client is a system; negotiate early who sits in, what"}, {"s": 0.59, "e": 0.11, "t": "is shared, and where the private space is. Stigma shapes disclosure: many clients arrive"}, {"s": 0.11, "e": 0.12, "t": "late with somatic complaints, because the body may speak what the mouth must not."}, {"s": 0.12, "e": 0.42, "t": "Language: Pidgin and mother tongue carry affect that English cannot; code-switch with"}, {"s": 0.42, "e": 0.95, "t": "the client rather than correct them. Logistics: crowded clinics and per-visit costs mean"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.95, "t": "brief, structured sessions, exactly what weeks five and six equipped you for. The"}, {"s": 0.95, "e": 0.92, "t": "relationship adapts; the function holds."}, {"s": 0.92, "e": 0.72, "t": "Gather the week. The relationship makes a substantial and consistent contribution to"}, {"s": 0.72, "e": 0.44, "t": "outcome, independent of method. Bordin's triad gives the working model; rupture and"}, {"s": 0.44, "e": 0.52, "t": "repair make the alliance trainable. The supported elements: empathy, regard, congruence,"}, {"s": 0.52, "e": 0.38, "t": "expectation, countertransference management, and cultural adaptation across them all."}, {"s": 0.38, "e": 0.32, "t": "ADDRESSING maps the person; awareness, knowledge and skills form the posture; advocacy"}, {"s": 0.32, "e": 0.63, "t": "keeps the gradient honest. It is the relationship that heals, and in Nigerian"}, {"s": 0.63, "e": 0.7, "t": "conditions, the culturally adapted relationship that heals."}, {"s": 0.7, "e": 0.29, "t": "Your tasks lead into the week-eight test. First, the alliance audit: rewatch your"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.29, "t": "microskills recording three times, once for bonds, once for goals, once for tasks; note"}, {"s": 0.29, "e": 0.3, "t": "one moment of strain and one of repair in each pass. Second, the identity exercise: map"}, {"s": 0.3, "e": 0.37, "t": "yourself on the nine ADDRESSING axes and mark where power flows toward you relative to a"}, {"s": 0.37, "e": 0.24, "t": "typical client in your future setting; write one paragraph on the axis you understand"}, {"s": 0.24, "e": 0.1, "t": "least, and one concrete way to learn it. Third, test preparation: the week-eight test"}, {"s": 0.1, "e": 0.97, "t": "covers weeks one to seven, worth fifteen per cent, and asks you to apply, not recite;"}, {"s": 0.97, "e": 0.14, "t": "practise explaining the conceptualisation chain, the alliance triad and the"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.14, "t": "multicultural triad to a study partner in two minutes each. Read Corey on the person of"}, {"s": 0.14, "e": 0.08, "t": "the counselor and the Sue and Sue introduction. Next week: mid-semester review and the"}, {"s": 0.08, "e": 0.46, "t": "test. See you there."}], "mode": "narrated", "duration": 772.46, "video": "/dist/CPY701-W07-lecture.mp4", "vtt": "/dist/w07-captions.vtt"}]};
